.nf
YASMV manual                                           check-progress

check-progress EXPR [ -states N ] [ -wall-ms N ] [ -c EXPR ] [ -async ]

Checks whether every execution eventually visits EXPR. Defaults: 10000 states,
30000 ms. Also accepts -conflicts N and -propagations N. Named goals are accepted.
No fairness is assumed. Dead ends and cycles before the goal violate progress.
Resource exhaustion is UNKNOWN. Empty initialization is explicitly vacuous.
Use dump-trace to inspect a failure and export-progress to save full evidence.
